## Phase 5 — N execution(s) block "Mark as Released" on <release>

Release: <base_url>/projects/<slug>/releases/<id>

### 1. Executions blocking closure

| Execution | Suite | Run | Outcome | Classification | Resolution to choose | Remediation reference |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| <cycle id> | <suite> | <run URL> | <failed / timed_out> | <flake / test bug / seed-data gap / defect fixed forward / defect open> | <retry_passed / superseded / accepted_exception / incident_remediated> | <tracking issue, incident or fix PR URL> |

### 2. Git steps (only for `accepted_exception`; do these first)

1. Open a tracking issue labelled `accepted-e2e-failure` holding the fix plan: <issue URL>.
2. Copy `references/e2e-accepted-failure.md.template` to `compliance/evidence/<REQ>/accepted-e2e-failure-<spec>.md` and fill it in.
3. Check it: `bash scripts/validate-risk-acceptance-record.sh --kind e2e compliance/evidence/<REQ>/accepted-e2e-failure-<spec>.md`.
4. Regenerate `test-execution-summary.md`: `devaudit release status <REQ> --json > /tmp/release-status.json && bash scripts/render-test-executions.sh /tmp/release-status.json`, then `bash scripts/validate-test-summary.sh`.
5. Land the record through a PR into `$INTEGRATION_BRANCH` (`Ref: <REQ>`).

### 3. Portal step (a project admin, after the git steps)

Open the release page above → journey panel → each execution in the table → choose the resolution in the table. Reason: name the committed record. Remediation reference: the tracking issue or incident URL. A project admin does this; the uploader key and this session cannot.

### 4. Order

git record → portal resolution → re-read `devaudit release status <REQ> --json` (every execution has a `resolution_type`) → **Approve Production** → **Mark as Released**.
